---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import { href } from '../lib/url'
import { links } from '../data/site'

const release = 'v0.2.0'
const dmg = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}/Nova-Studio-0.2.0-arm64.dmg`
const exe = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}/Nova-Studio-0.2.0-x64-setup.exe`
const cli = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}/nova-0.2.0-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz`
const vsix = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}/nova-language-0.2.0.vsix`
const sums = `https://github.com/jd4rider/nova/releases/download/${release}/SHA256SUMS`
---
<SiteLayout title="Install" path="install" description="Install Nova Studio and the Nova language with Homebrew, macOS DMG, Windows EXE, VS Code extension or from source.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> v0.2.0 preview · unsigned installers</span>
      <h1>Install Nova.</h1>
      <p>Get the native Rust language and Nova Studio together with one Homebrew command, use a direct installer, install the VS Code extension, or build the whole toolchain from source.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions" style="margin-top: 26px;">
        <a class="button primary" href="#homebrew">Install with Homebrew</a>
        <a class="button" href="#vscode">VS Code extension</a>
        <a class="button" href={href('getting-started/installation/')}>Read the detailed guide</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="homebrew" style="padding-top: 18px;">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose" style="max-width: none;">
        <div class="kicker">Recommended · macOS arm64</div>
        <h2>Studio and language, together.</h2>
        <p>The public Homebrew tap installs both the <code>nova</code> compiler/CLI and Nova Studio. The Studio cask declares the language formula as a dependency, so one command gets both.</p>
        <pre><code>brew install --cask jd4rider/tap/nova-studio
nova --version
open -a "Nova Studio"</code></pre>
        <p>If Homebrew asks you to trust the tap:</p>
        <pre><code>brew trust jd4rider/tap</code></pre>
        <p>Language only:</p>
        <pre><code>brew install jd4rider/tap/nova</code></pre>
        <p>Nova links native programs with the host Clang. Install the Xcode Command Line Tools if needed:</p>
        <pre><code>xcode-select --install</code></pre>
      </div>
      <aside class="card">
        <div class="kicker">What the cask installs</div>
        <table class="status-table">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Nova language</td><td><code>nova</code> CLI + compiler from the tap</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Nova Studio</td><td><code>/Applications/Nova Studio.app</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Architecture</td><td>macOS arm64</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Signing</td><td><span class="badge planned">unsigned</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Updates</td><td>Manual <code>brew upgrade</code> / new DMG</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 13px; margin-top: 16px;">The cask does not bypass Gatekeeper. If macOS blocks first launch, right-click → Open, or clear quarantine for the app only.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker">Direct installers</div>
          <h2>DMG and NSIS EXE.</h2>
          <p class="section-intro">These are real artifacts built from the tagged source by electron-builder. They are preview-quality and unsigned.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="button" href={sums} rel="noreferrer">SHA-256 checksums ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="grid-3">
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">⌘</div>
          <h3>macOS arm64 DMG</h3>
          <p>Nova Studio 0.2.0, 115 MB. Drag the app to Applications. The DMG installs Studio only; install the language with Homebrew or source.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href={dmg} rel="noreferrer">Download DMG ↓</a>
          <div class="meta">Apple silicon · unsigned</div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">⊞</div>
          <h3>Windows x64 EXE</h3>
          <p>Nova Studio 0.2.0 NSIS installer, 94 MB. Assisted installer with Start Menu and desktop shortcuts. The CLI is not bundled.</p>
          <a class="button primary" href={exe} rel="noreferrer">Download EXE ↓</a>
          <div class="meta">Windows x64 · unsigned · pipe terminal</div>
        </article>
        <article class="card">
          <div class="card-icon" aria-hidden="true">fn</div>
          <h3>macOS CLI archive</h3>
          <p>Standalone <code>nova</code> 0.2.0 binary for Apple silicon, with a README and no installer. Verify with the release checksums.</p>
          <a class="button" href={cli} rel="noreferrer">Download CLI ↓</a>
          <div class="meta">macOS arm64 · 852 KB</div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="notice danger" style="margin-top: 20px;"><strong>Unsigned preview:</strong> the app is not Developer ID signed or notarized and the EXE is not Authenticode signed. macOS may require right-click → Open; Windows SmartScreen may require <strong>More info → Run anyway</strong>. Checksums are published, but checksums are not code signing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="vscode">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose" style="max-width: none;">
        <div class="kicker">Use your own editor</div>
        <h2>Nova in VS Code.</h2>
        <p>The <strong>Nova Language</strong> extension adds <code>.nova</code> syntax highlighting and launches the same Rust language server as Studio. It does not require the Studio app.</p>
        <pre><code>code --install-extension nova-language-0.2.0.vsix</code></pre>
        <p>Download the VSIX and use the terminal command above, or open <strong>Extensions → … → Install from VSIX…</strong> in VS Code.</p>
        <a class="button primary" href={vsix} rel="noreferrer">Download VSIX ↓</a>
        <p style="margin-top: 18px;">Syntax highlighting works without the compiler. For diagnostics, completion, hover, definitions, symbols and formatting, install the <code>nova</code> CLI with Homebrew and make sure VS Code can find it:</p>
        <pre><code>brew install jd4rider/tap/nova
nova --version</code></pre>
        <p>If VS Code was launched from the GUI and cannot see your shell PATH, set <code>nova.serverPath</code> to the absolute binary path. The extension has a <strong>Nova: Restart Language Server</strong> command and writes failures to <strong>Output → Nova Language Server</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Extension status</div>
        <table class="status-table">
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Syntax</td><td>Shared TextMate grammar for <code>.nova</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td>LSP</td><td>Diagnostics, completion, hover, definitions, symbols, formatting</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Distribution</td><td><span class="badge implemented">local VSIX</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Marketplace</td><td><span class="badge planned">not published</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Tested with</td><td>VS Code 1.143.1 on macOS arm64</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 13px; margin-top: 16px;">The extension is platform-independent, but the language server needs a built <code>nova</code> binary. The published prebuilt CLI is macOS arm64; other platforms build from source.</p>
        <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 13px;">The server currently uses full-document sync and single-file indexing. No debugger, task runner or Extension Host automation is included yet.</p>
        <a class="button" href={href('toolchain/vscode/')}>Extension documentation →</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap grid-2" style="align-items: start;">
      <div class="prose" style="max-width: none;">
        <div class="kicker">Build from source</div>
        <h2>No binaries required.</h2>
        <p>You need Rust 1.96+, Cargo and Clang. Node 20+ is only needed for Studio or the website.</p>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/jd4rider/nova.git
cd nova
cargo build --release -p nova-cli
export PATH="$PWD/target/release:$PATH"
nova --version
nova doctor</code></pre>
        <p>Build a program and Studio:</p>
        <pre><code>nova new hello
cd hello
nova run
cd ../editor
npm ci --no-audit --no-fund
NOVA_BIN="$PWD/../target/release/nova" npm run dev</code></pre>
      </div>
      <aside class="card">
        <div class="kicker">Platform matrix</div>
        <table class="status-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Platform</th><th>Installer</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>macOS arm64</td><td>DMG / brew</td><td><span class="badge tested">built + mounted</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Windows x64</td><td>NSIS EXE</td><td><span class="badge implemented">built</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>macOS arm64</td><td>CLI archive</td><td><span class="badge tested">smoke-tested</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>macOS x64</td><td>source only</td><td><span class="badge planned">no prebuilt</span></td></tr>
            <tr><td>Linux</td><td>source only</td><td><span class="badge planned">no prebuilt</span></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="section-intro" style="font-size: 13px; margin-top: 16px;">Windows Studio was cross-built and structurally verified; it has not been launched on a Windows host. No Intel/Linux installer is published.</p>
        <a class="button" href={links.releases} rel="noreferrer">All release assets ↗</a>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="cta"><div><div class="kicker">Next</div><h2>Compile your first project.</h2><p>Start with the checked hello-world example and the project layout.</p></div><a class="button primary" href={href('getting-started/hello-world/')}>Get started →</a></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>
